    "done_when": "At the dispatch base 5337225ba, scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit sets hook_root with git -C on its own directory followed by rev-parse --show-toplevel. Inside a linked worktree git exports GIT_DIR, and GIT_WORK_TREE is unset or relative, while a hook runs, so that rev-parse returns the hooks directory and the hook refuses every commit made from a worktree. (1) Resolve the checkout root from the hook's own location without consulting git: realpath -e the script, then take its directory's parent's parent with cd and pwd -P. Keep the hook a read-only shim that runs the checkout's .venv/bin/python3 on nova.database.scripts with relativize --check and PYTHONPATH set to that root. (2) Add tests/test_commit_hook_in_worktree.py. It builds a small scratch git repository under tmp_path with a linked worktree from git worktree add, and core.hooksPath pointing at a copy of the hook. Make the hook's nova import resolvable without copying the whole repository, for example by placing nova as a symlink to the real package directory and .venv/bin/python3 as a symlink to /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python3. Then commit from the linked worktree: a clean file is admitted, and a file naming a nova worktree path is refused naming that file. Also commit once from the scratch main checkout, to show both still work. Gate: JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_commit_hook_in_worktree.py, run from the worktree with PYTHONPATH set to the worktree, passes, logged with EXIT=. Negative control, logged: the same test against the base hook fails on the linked-worktree clean commit. Do not set core.hooksPath in any real checkout; the coordinator re-enables it after landing. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. Report to /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s27/acnwp-hook-worktree-root.md.",
    "estimated_hours": 0.5,
